.\" man page create by R# package system.
.TH ARACNE 1 2000-1月 "aracne_options" "aracne_options"
.SH NAME
aracne_options \- Create an [AracneOptions](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Model.Network.Regulons.ARACNE.AracneOptions) object from the scalar arguments.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIaracne_options(\fBestimator\fR as string = "copula", 
\fBthreshold\fR as string = "permutation", 
\fBmi_cutoff\fR as double = 0, 
\fBquantile\fR as double = 0.95, 
\fBpermutations\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBdpi\fR as string = "auto", 
\fBepsilon\fR as double = 0.1, 
\fBdirection\fR as string = "tf", 
\fBbins\fR as integer = 4, 
\fBmax_neighbors\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBmax_genes\fR as integer = 0, 
\fBmin_nonzero\fR as double = 0, 
\fBlog2\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBrank\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBstandardize\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBprior_min_confidence\fR as double = 0.45, 
\fBprior_factor\fR as double = 0.5, 
\fBprior_protection\fR as string = "graded", 
\fBprior_strength\fR as double = 0.5, 
\fBprior_tf_augment\fR as boolean = TRUE, 
\fBthreads\fR as integer = -1, 
\fBseed\fR as integer = 1234567, 
\fBsilent\fR as boolean = TRUE);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Create an [AracneOptions](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Model.Network.Regulons.ARACNE.AracneOptions) object from the scalar arguments.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBestimator\fB \fR\- 
 the mutual information estimator: \fBcopula\fR (default, \fBO(n)\fR per gene pair),
 \fBadaptive\fR (the adaptive partitioning of the ARACNE paper), \fBhistogram\fR
 (equal frequency bins with the Miller-Madow correction) or \fBkernel\fR
 (gaussian kernel density, \fBO(n^2)\fR).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBthreshold\fB \fR\- 
 \fBpermutation\fR (default, the quantile of the null distribution that is created
 by shuffling the samples of each gene) or \fBfixed\fR (use **mi_cutoff**).
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmi_cutoff\fB \fR\- 
 the fixed mutual information threshold; a positive value forces the \fBfixed\fR
 mode even when **threshold** is \fBpermutation\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBquantile\fB \fR\- the quantile of the permutation null distribution, default 0.95. 
.PP
.PP
\fBpermutations\fB \fR\- 
 the number of the gene pairs that are sampled for the null distribution,
 a value that is less than or equals to 0 means "auto".
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdpi\fB \fR\- 
 \fBauto\fR (TF guided when a TF list is given, otherwise standard),
 \fBstandard\fR, \fBtf\fR (TF guided) or \fBoff\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBepsilon\fB \fR\- the DPI tolerance, default 0.1. 
.PP
.PP
\fBdirection\fB \fR\- \fBtf\fR (default) or \fBundirected\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBbins\fB \fR\- the bin number of the \fBhistogram\fR estimator, default 4. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmax_neighbors\fB \fR\- 
 the max number of the edges that each regulator can keep (top-K pruning),
 a value that is less than or equals to 0 means "no pruning".
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmax_genes\fB \fR\- 
 keep only the top variant genes; the genes of the TF list and of the prior
 network are always kept.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmin_nonzero\fB \fR\- the minimal ratio of the non-zero samples for a gene to be kept. 
.PP
.PP
\fBlog2\fB \fR\- apply a \fBlog2(x + 1)\fR transformation before the inference. 
.PP
.PP
\fBrank\fB \fR\- use the ranks (spearman) instead of the values (pearson). 
.PP
.PP
\fBstandardize\fB \fR\- z-score the expression vectors before the inference. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior_min_confidence\fB \fR\- 
 the eligibility threshold of the curated prior edges, default 0.45 (i.e. Low and above)
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior_factor\fB \fR\- 
 the threshold relaxation factor at the full confidence, default 0.5;
 the prior edge of the confidence \fBc\fR uses \fBtau * (1 - (1 - factor) * c)\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior_protection\fB \fR\- 
 \fBgraded\fR (default: the DPI protection window is scaled by the confidence),
 \fBsampled\fR (a prior edge is fully protected with the probability \fBp = c\fR)
 or \fBoff\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior_strength\fB \fR\- the strength of the graded protection, default 0.5. 
.PP
.PP
\fBprior_tf_augment\fB \fR\- 
 append the regulators of the prior network into the TF set, so that a incomplete
 TF annotation does not lose the regulation edges.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBthreads\fB \fR\- the max degree of parallelism, a value that is less than or equals to 0 means "auto". 
.PP
.PP
\fBseed\fB \fR\- the random seed of the permutation sampling and of the sampled protection. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsilent\fB \fR\- do not print the progress messages. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the options object that can be used by the \fBinfer\fR api
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
ARACNE
.SH FILES
.PP
TRNtoolkit.dll
.PP
